  "genre": "Sacred Hindu Epic / Classical Meitei Translation & Narrative",
  "description": "The eternal Hindu epic Mahabharata with emphasis on its renowned historical and sacred connection to ancient Manipur. Chronicles the conflict between the Pandavas and Kauravas, the philosophical wisdom of the Bhagavad Gita spoken by Lord Krishna, Arjuna's sacred pilgrimage to ancient Manipur where he wed warrior princess Chitrangada, the valor of their son King Babruvahana who held the sacrificial horse of the Ashvamedha Yajna, and the ultimate triumph of Dharma on the plains of Kurukshetra. An integral part of Manipuri Wari Leeba oral narration and court literature since the 18th century.",
  "source": "Manipuri Mahabharata Manuscripts (Ashvamedha Parva & Virata Parva adaptations), Royal Court Archives of Manipur, and Wari Leeba oral traditions",
  "copyright": "Public Domain (Traditional Meitei Epic Adaptation and Cultural Heritage)",
